WEBVTT

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.480
<b>Home Economics Room</b>

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.860
I feel like it was sweeter.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.380
Do I just add more sugar?

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.370
Hey, Yuu!

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.460
How many bowls are you trying to feed us?

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.630
We can't eat any more!

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.630
What? Can't you eat just one more bowl?

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.360
Nope.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.500
Thanks for the food.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
I think this is already a great ramen.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.800
What aren't you satisfied with?

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.860
No, this is totally different.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:38.680
I remember that tasty ramen I ate 
in Osaka when I was a little kid.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.040
I think the place was close 
to my grandma's house.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.300
Last night, as I was falling asleep, 
it just popped into my head.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.270
Thank you for waiting.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.640
It's so good!

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.910
Yum!

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.840
I've been hoping to replicate that 
taste to entice Koizumi-san over.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.290
It's so amazing that you can 
make ramen this delicious.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.760
Let's be friends.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.070
I would love to!

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.580
Why does that sound...

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.340
...easier said than done?

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:25.540
Unfortunately, I can't remember the 
ramen clearly enough to replicate it.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.930
Do you at least know the name 
of the restaurant? Or their menu?

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:32.320
I was really little, so I don't remember.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.880
And it's in Osaka, so I can't 
just take her to it, either.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.960
Why don't you ask someone 
in your family, then?

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.160
Maybe your brother?

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.620
That's our Jun! So smart!

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.290
<b>Yuu</b>

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.290
<b>Brother, this is an emergency.
Do you remember the ramen we 
ate in Osaka back then? You know, 
when we had that rare outing where 
we all went, back when I had 
just entered kindergarten.</b>

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.290
<b>What kind of ramen
was that again?</b>

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.290
<b>Please tell me</b>

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.630
Oh, it's from Yuu.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.240
Your sister?

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.800
Yeah... "Brother, get back to me right away."

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:59.300
<b>Yuu: Brother, this is an emergency.
Do you remember the ramen we 
ate in Osaka back then? You know, 
when we had that rare outing where 
we all went,back when I had 
just entered kindergarten.</b>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:59.300
<b>Yuu: What kind of ramen
was that again?</b>

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.060
<i>Do you remember the ramen 
we ate in Osaka back then?</i>

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:59.300
<b>Please tell me</b>

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.300
<i>You know, when we all went, 
back when I was in kindergarten.</i>

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.560
<i>"What kind of ramen was that again?"</i>

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.030
<i>"Please tell me."</i>

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.310
Oh, yeah, that ramen. I know.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.060
<b>Ping</b>

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.190
He wrote back!

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.310
I knew he'd come through.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.070
<b>Bro: Oh, sure. That was</b>

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.360
<i>Oh, sure. That was...</i>

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.070
<b>Bro: Tasty Ramen</b>

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.070
<i>Tasty Ramen.</i>

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.200
Yuu

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.200
<b>I'm not asking
for your opinion</b>

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.200
<i>I'm not asking for your opinion.</i>

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.040
What the heck?! What's wrong with Yuu?!

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.170
Why is Ohsawa crying?

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.200
I told her, and this is how she treats me?!

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.200
Who knows? Sibling fight?

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.150
I can't count on him.

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.210
I'm going to have to remember it myself.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.530
Uh, it had some kind of leafy vegetable 
and some kind of chopped meat...

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:40.880
The soup had a gentle sweetness, 
kind of like sukiyaki sauce.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.220
It wasn't a particularly light flavor, though.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.850
Anyway, it was a tasty ramen.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.480
That's not exactly enough info.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.440
Tasty ramen?

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.860
Staaare...

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.190
K-Koizumi-san?!

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:56.020
Excuse me. I don't actually 
have any business here,

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.430
but I was walking down the hall,
and I smelled ramen.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.030
Yeah, okay! So come on in!

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.960
I can't believe this is actually working.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.880
Here, have a seat!

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.370
Excuse me.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.540
It's... still a work in progress.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.690
Thank you for the food.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:41.670
By the way, you were talking about 
a ramen that this was based on.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.700
Could it be...

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.200
Tasty Ramen?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.580
Huh? Yes, it was.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.830
Because their main branch is 
located in Osaka's Dotonbori,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.120
but Tokyo has a location, too.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.350
Wait, really?! Where?

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.840
I want to go there!

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.000
I don't think we can...

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.200
...eat any more ramen today.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:24.450
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:24.990
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:25.910
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:40.980
<b>Kabukicho Ichibangai</b>

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:40.980
<b>Tasty Ramen</b>

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:46.290
I think that's what you were talking about.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:47.990
Huh?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.030
Tasty Ramen

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.300
Tasty ramen!

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.980
Welcome!

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.820
Please take a seat anywhere you like.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.520
Two customers coming in!

00:05:58.520 --> 00:05:59.780
Welcome!

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:03.880
So I guess it's literally called 
"Tasty Ramen" on the menu.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.130
I'll have to text an apology to my brother.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:09.640
Excuse me.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.410
Here's your Tasty Ramen.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.890
Please add some garlic chives, if you like.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.650
Yes, this is the scent!

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:23.600
Time to eat.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.040
This is it! The napa cabbage 
gives it that gentle sweetness.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.090
But maybe it's the higher
amount of flavored oil

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.550
that keeps it from being too light?

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.020
<i>The soup is always so hot here.</i>

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.950
I guess these are the garlic chives?

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.460
<i>The garlic chives give it 
an even deeper flavor.</i>

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:27.800
Customers coming in.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.510
Welcome!

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.600
<b>Still hot</b>

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:54.380
<i>That really was tasty ramen!</i>

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:58.080
Thank you for the food.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.440
I just drank all that soup without thinking.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:07.300
I never thought I'd have the ramen of 
my childhood memories here in Tokyo.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.480
I was sure I'd have to go 
all the way to Osaka for it.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.170
Huh?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.610
Koizumi-san?

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.180
<b>Thank you</b>

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.160
What's wrong, Koizumi-san?

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.810
<b>— The Next Day —</b>

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:30.980
<b>Shin Osaka
Shin Osaka
Hiroshima
Shin Osaka
Hakata</b>

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:30.980
<b>Non-Reserved   Cars 1-3
Non-Reserved   Cars 1-3
Non-Reserved   Cars 1-3
Non-Reserved   Cars 1-3
Non-Reserved   Cars 1-3</b>

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:43.250
<b>Tokyo</b>

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:43.500
<b>Passenger Ticket - Bullet Train Non-Reserved Seat</b>

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:43.500
<b>Shin Osaka</b>

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:42.740
It's been a while since I went west.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:46.070
It was Tasty Ramen.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:47.920
It was Tasty Ramen, was it not?

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.400
It was tasty ramen!

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.010
It was tasty ramen, was it not?!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.010
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:04.010
<b>Osaka</b>

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.770
<b>Menya Joroku</b>

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.800
Time to eat.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.060
<b>- The Next Day -</b>

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.560
Hey, hey, girlie! Hey, hey, hey!

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.790
Where ya goin'?

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:53.520
If you're free, wanna hang?

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:56.750
We know some really good places. Eh, eh?

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:59.950
<b>The
10th
time
on
this
bridge
alone</b>

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.570
<i>I can't move forward.</i>

00:09:58.570 --> 00:09:59.950
Oh, there you are!

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:04.290
Sorry I'm late, Charlotte!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.620
Shall we?

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.800
Hey, wait!

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:09.330
Just hear me out!

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:13.550
Excuse me, but who is Charlotte?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.550
And... who are you?

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:20.480
Ya just looked like a Charlotte.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:23.960
I felt bad for ya, since those 
guys kept hittin' on ya.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.360
Thank you for helping me out.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:29.360
I'll be going now.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.000
Hey, wait!

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.660
You were at a ramen place 
in Nanba last night, yeah?

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:37.190
I could tell from your accent 
that you're from Tokyo.

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.070
At the restaurant last night...

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:40.790
Oh, miss, you can just leave it.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:41.980
Oh, force of habit.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:45.210
After ya finished, ya put your 
bowl up on the counter.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:47.950
That's not somethin' folks
from around here would do.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.210
You're in high school, right?

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:52.560
Tourin' Osaka by yourself?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.460
I came here to eat ramen.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:00.550
Whoa, whoa... It might be 
weird for a local to say this,

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.720
but Osaka ramen really ain't that big a deal.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.840
We don't have anything unique here, either.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.410
I don't see what brought ya from Kanto—

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.350
Untrue.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.190
Osaka's ramen... is definitely 
the thing right now.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.200
Of course there are the established places,

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:19.650
but there's also a lot of new places 
with potential coming onto the scene.

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:23.400
You just said that this 
area doesn't have its own

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.040
distinct style of noodles, but there's 
the type called "Takaida."

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.560
Yesterday's chuuka soba is 
derived from that genre,

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.900
and the further development 
of that rich soy sauce base

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:33.880
is "Osaka Black," which is
one of my favorites.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:38.540
Anyway, this is my last day in Osaka.

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:39.840
I still have four more bowls to go.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:39.840
Wait!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.460
Hey, hey, where are you going!

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:46.600
<b>Can't move yet again</b>

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:43.160
Hey, you wanna hang out?

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.800
Hey, hey...

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.600
I told ya so.

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.560
<b>Was saved again</b>

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:54.250
This is just a suggestion, 
but I could be your bodyguard!

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.730
So let me tag along today.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.360
Hey!

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:57.230
<b>Hey</b>

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:57.610
<b>Hey</b>

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.040
Hey!

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:57.940
<b>Hey</b>

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:58.280
<b>Hey</b>

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:58.610
Hey!

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:58.570
<b>Hey</b>

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:58.610
<b>Hey</b>

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.920
Thank you.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:01.860
Yes!

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:06.370
My name is Ayane and I'm 25 years old,
a Virgo, and blood type O!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.710
How about you?

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.060
My name is Koizumi.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.480
Koizumi-chan!

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.120
Let's be friends!

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:14.250
Let's be friends!

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:15.710
Déjà vu.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.960
I'm sorry about this.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:23.380
But I did want to try Osaka's tasty ramen,
and it's my last day, too.

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.390
<b>Tori Paitan
Ramen</b>

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.390
<b>Bokkoshi</b>

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:29.860
Welcome!

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.180
Thank you for waiting!

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:35.380
One tori paitan and one
extra thick tori paitan.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.020
It's so white! Why?

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.940
Weren't ya talkin' about 
some black stuff earlier?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:44.380
I already visited all the soy sauce 
based restaurants yesterday.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.280
Today, I'm focusing on newly opened stores.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:52.040
Osaka's "whites," like tori paitan 
and salt ramen, are hot, too.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.540
I dunno about that, but I guess 
there are all kinds of ramen.

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:59.280
I haven't done this since 
I entered the workforce.

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:00.880
Time to eat!

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.600
This is so good!

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.810
What is this?

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.190
It's so rich and creamy!

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:13.770
Please eat more quietly.

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:22.980
<b>Thanks for eating 
our ramen.</b>

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.980
That was so good!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.840
That paitan ramen was so milky!
I could get hooked on that, all right!

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.670
Incidentally, they don't use 
milk to make it white.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.250
Oh, really?

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:39.110
The white soup that results from a long, 
hot cooking process is called paitan.

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:44.380
The clear soup that results from
low-temperature cooking is called chintan.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.130
I see.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.600
I didn't know they taught stuff 
like that in Tokyo high schools.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.930
I didn't learn this in school.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.900
<b>Ramen</b>

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.950
Look at this sparkling salt broth!

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:05.860
Two types of char siu 
made from local chickens.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.320
Superb.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.040
<b>R
a
m
e
n</b>

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.040
<b>T
s
u
k
e
m
e
n</b>

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.040
<b>R
a
m
e
n</b>

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.040
<b>T
s
u
k
e
m
e
n</b>

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.040
<b>Men no 
Youji</b>

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.040
<b>Parents                           Kids                    Grandkids</b>

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:22.040
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:28.510
Just look at this beautiful soup!

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:37.270
The umami from the vegetables and 
chicken is permeatin' my entire body!

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.440
I'm so full!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.770
I can't believe I've eaten 
four bowls for lunch.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:45.450
Are you going to be okay?

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:46.480
Yes!

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:50.280
I come from a family with big stomachs, 
thanks to my grandmother.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:53.780
But after all that,
you're still having takoyaki?

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.540
Well, I am in Osaka.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:59.920
Boy, eatin' that ramen made 
me want to get a drink.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.930
Why don't you go get a drink, then?

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:05.380
I can't join you, since I'm underage.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:07.800
I'll pass.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:12.820
It's better to not drink somethin' 
you love when you're all gloomy.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:15.310
Y'know...

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.200
I quit my job.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:23.120
After this, I'll be workin' a job in 
Tokyo that my relatives got me.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:26.320
So this is my last day in Osaka.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:29.990
I was doin' stuff I liked for a living,

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:32.240
but it was starting to be too stressful.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:37.380
Yesterday, I asked my friends to go out 
with me to get my mind off things,

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:41.750
but I couldn't really enjoy the drinks.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.560
Then, on my way home,
I remembered a ramen place

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.160
I used to go to after drinkin'.

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:48.250
I hadn't been there in so long.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.980
It was the best.

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:54.740
Why does the ramen you eat 
after some drinks taste so good?

00:15:55.900 --> 00:16:00.200
Paitan and salt ramen are good, too,
but I guess I prefer soy sauce based ones.

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:02.390
The simple kind with naruto 
and stuff on them.

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:06.520
When I was in college, the place 
I often went to was in Tsurumi.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.400
I could never forget that taste.

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:13.460
I forgot the name of the store, 
though. What was it again?

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:16.410
Then let's go there next.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:18.680
I want to try it now, too.

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:19.430
Huh?

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.490
You're really gonna take me there?

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:22.910
Thank you!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:32.130
<b>Chuuka Soba</b>

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:29.160
Hey, this isn't Tsurumi.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:29.840
I'm going in.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.130
Koizumi-chan, wait!

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:34.780
Excuse me. Here's your chuuka soba.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.310
Thank you for waiting.

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:39.880
This does kind of look like that ramen.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:41.100
Time to eat.

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:42.980
Time to eat!

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:52.600
This is it!

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:55.430
This unpretentious, simple chuuka soba!

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:59.180
Some years ago, the main restaurant 
transferred over here.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:01.660
What's in Tsurumi now is a branch location.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.580
So that's why we're here.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:08.980
The location may be new, but it 
tastes just as good as before.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:13.590
If anything, it tastes 
even better than before.

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:18.970
The longer a store has been in business,
the more it's devoted to improving its ramen.

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.220
It looks the same,

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.670
but it's continuously changing.

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:35.610
If I ate this after some drinks, 
it'd be even more delicious!

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:40.580
This is the last place.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:44.500
The last place is in the office 
district? That's just cold.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:47.320
Ya know I just quit my job.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:50.580
I simply wanted to eat this black ramen, too.

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:52.000
There was no other reason.

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:56.210
More importantly, I thought you 
shouldn't drink when you're gloomy?

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:58.670
Oh, well, they had drinks on the menu!

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.890
No, that's not it.

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:17.060
The day before I start my new journey,

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:20.300
I've been eatin' delicious 
ramen with a cute li'l lady

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:23.560
all over the city that I've
called home for 25 years.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:29.700
I left gloomy behind me a long 
time ago. I'm in a great mood!

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:37.240
The reason I quit my company was 
because I didn't wanna stop working.

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:39.010
Isn't that a contradiction?

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.880
That's right, bein' an adult 
is all about contradictions.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:45.010
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:47.020
One Kurofune.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:50.860
All right, then!

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:52.360
Time to eat.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.430
Yum!

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:13.000
Black ramen really is the best.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.960
Not all black ramens are the same.

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:20.590
Thanks for spendin' today with me.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:21.340
Here ya go.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:23.560
It's my contact information.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.050
I'll be counting on you in Tokyo.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:27.830
For what, exactly?

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:33.860
Oh, yeah! I've got a cousin the 
same age as you over there.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:33.860
<b>Ohsawa Ayane</b>

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:35.510
You don't mean—

00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:38.530
She's comin' out today to help me move.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:41.080
She should be here soon. I'll introduce ya.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.640
No... I...

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.200
C'mon, let's go!

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.080
Koizumi-san!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.180
Yuu!

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:50.800
I knew it.

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.190
What are you doing in Osaka?

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:53.290
You ignored me?!

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.440
I would've never expected to meet you here.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.990
What are you two doing together, anyway?

00:19:57.990 --> 00:20:00.230
I was just about to ask you the same thing.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:01.670
You know each other?

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:05.000
Koizumi-chan's been showing 
me around all day.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.330
What?! Do that for me, too!

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.890
Time to get on my train.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.420
Koizumi-chan! Let's meet again in Tokyo!

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:15.020
Hey! Wait!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.430
Hey, Aya-neechan.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:18.230
Where's Yuu?

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:19.300
Over there.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:24.340
Koizumi-san!

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:27.030
<b>Yuu (5 years old)</b>

00:20:25.690 --> 00:20:29.840
Aya-neechan, there's a dragon 
stuck in the ramen place!

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:30.540
<b>Kinryuu</b>

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:32.640
That's Naniwa's guardian deity.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.790
<b>Thank goodness!</b>

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.410
Oh, a guardian deity.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.050
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Nagoya</b>

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:30.030
<b>Reunion</b>

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:14.850
Looks like you're pretty used 
to Osaka, huh, Koizumi-chan?

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:16.680
I've been there many times.

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:19.760
Well, then, why don't you try 
speakin' in in the Osaka dialect?

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:20.610
What for?

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:24.200
I wanna hear your adorable voice 
speaking in the Osaka dialect!

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:26.580
Oh, come on, please?

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:28.140
I'm thinkin' not.

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:29.540
You're a native speaker!

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:36.040
<b>Thank you for the meal!</b>
